= President Zamora sacks Azaña's Government

The aftermath of Casas Viejas, combined with bad municipal election results in April and fierce parliamentary obstruction by the right, has exhausted Manuel Azaña's government. President Niceto Alcalá-Zamora, increasingly hostile to the left's reformist pace, withdraws his confidence from Azaña and forces his resignation on June 8.

However, Alcalá-Zamora's attempt to find an alternative majority fails after Alejandro Lerroux refuses to form a government with socialist support. Left with no other viable parliamentary combination, Alcalá-Zamora is reluctantly forced to reappoint Manuel Azaña to form his Third Cabinet.

The crisis triggers a fierce battle inside the Radical Socialist Party (PRRS). Félix Gordón Ordás leads the conservative wing, demanding an immediate break with the PSOE to form a centrist bloc alongside Lerroux's PRR. Meanwhile, Marcelino Domingo defends coalition discipline and loyalty to the reformist alliance with the socialists.

[? if prrs_relation >= 65 and psoe_in_government == 1 : Thanks to our strong historical partnership, Marcelino Domingo's faction retains control of the party executive, renewing their commitment to the Republican-Socialist Conjunction. ?]
[? if prrs_relation < 65 : Due to growing resentment and strained relations, Félix Gordón Ordás wins the internal debate. The PRRS officially breaks with the left-wing bloc, refusing further coalition ties with the PSOE! ?]

