@support_marcelino
title: Enter Azaña's Third Cabinet alongside Marcelino Domingo.
view-if: prrs_relation >= 65 and psoe_in_government == 1
on-arrival: prrs_relation += 5; ar_relation += 5; caballeristas_dissent += 5; workers_psoe -= 3; middle_psoe += 3;

We maintain our ministries, ensuring that the Agrarian Reform and public education programs continue. 

However, Gordón Ordás' supporters form an internal opposition movement (*Partido Radical Socialista Independiente*), signaling that the PRRS is on the verge of an inevitable schism.

- @continue: Continue governing.

@gordon_split
title: Gordón Ordás takes control of the PRRS and breaks the coalition.
view-if: prrs_relation < 65
on-arrival: prrs_relation -= 15; pro_republic -= 5; prrs_leader = "Gordón Ordás"

Gordón Ordás and the majority of the PRRS parliamentary group announce their withdrawal from the left-wing coalition, seeking closer ties with Alejandro Lerroux's Radical Party. 

Without the PRRS, Azaña's Third Cabinet is born dead, operating as a fragile minority government while facing a hostile parliamentary majority. Left-wing republican unity is shattered, making any future coalition with the PRRS practically impossible.

- @continue: The government won't last long.